  "notes": [
    "The three pinned cores expose the same call topology for both Category Colors update_option(name, value, true) and Tribe__Cache::set_last_occurrence update_option(name, value) paths.",
    "wp_default_autoload_value and wp_max_autoloaded_option_size are unreachable for Category Colors explicit autoload=true but reachable for absent or computed-autoload tribe_last_save_post rows.",
    "The stock cache.php and class-wp-object-cache.php bytes are identical across all three pins and expose no callback hook around wp_cache_get/set/delete; external object-cache drop-ins are refused before invocation.",
    "The exact TEC 6.17.2 and 6.17.3 Category Colors, Customizer, cache/listener/container, option-hook singleton, configuration, event/occurrence/builder, occurrence-generator, and widget storage classes are pinned. The widget Service_Provider intentionally differs: 6.17.3 adds recursive object refusal before its copy/save/render callbacks re-sign an embedded legacy-widget instance.",
    "Tribe__Customizer registers its legacy read only on default_option_tribe_customizer: an existing canonical row wins even when it stores an empty array, while an absent canonical row may fall back to tribe_events_pro_customizer. The legacy name is compatibility input, not a claim that this free adapter supports Pro.",
    "The exact four free Views V2 Customizer services register 31 option-backed settings across global_elements, month_view, tec_events_bar, and single_event. Raw storage is sparse: defaults are merged for reads and are not proof that a setting was persisted. Two view-selector keys remain referenced only by the shipped JavaScript and are known target-owned upgrade residue, not free server-side authored settings.",
    "A normal TEC core/legacy-widget block is state-bearing in either form: id points through SidebarState to sidebars_widgets plus widget_<idBase>, while idBase plus instance embeds base64 PHP-serialized settings and an environment-salted hash. Exact 6.17.3 security hardening does not make those bytes portable by itself; the adapter remains unready until it validates and rebinds both forms."
  ]
}
